{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "Butterflies Lingering Over Flowers

I lean alone on the tall building where the breeze blows fine,
Gazing far into the distance, a spring sorrow
Dimly rises at the edge of the sky.

In the fading light, the grass is veined with misty glow;
Silent, who can understand my leaning on the rail?

I mean to seek release in wild abandon, and get drunk;
Facing wine and singing, forced merriment still lacks flavor.

My clothes grow loose and wide, yet I feel no regret;
For her sake, I am willing to waste away."}

