{"source": {"title": "登高", "author": "杜甫", "text": "风急天高猿啸哀，渚清沙白鸟飞回。
无边落木萧萧下，不尽长江滚滚来。
万里悲秋常作客，百年多病独登台。
艰难苦恨繁霜鬓，潦倒新停浊酒杯。"}, "translation": "Ascending the Heights

By Du Fu

The wind is high, the sky is vast — the gibbons cry with sorrow;
The islet clear, the sand white — birds wheel in flight.
Boundless, the falling leaves come rustling down;
Endless, the Yangtze River comes rolling on.
Ten thousand miles away, grieving at autumn, forever a stranger;\nA hundred years of illness, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened the frost at my temples;
Down and out, I have just now set down my cup of turbid wine."}

{"source": {"title": "登高", "author": "杜甫", "text": "风急天高猿啸哀，渚清沙白鸟飞回。
