艰难苦恨繁霜鬓，潦倒新停浊酒杯。"}, "translation": "The wind is swift, the sky vast, apes wail in mournful cry; 
Isles clear, sand white, birds wheel back and soar. 
Boundless trees shed leaves with rustling sighs; 
Endless river rolls on, ceaseless, roaring. 
A thousand miles of sorrow in autumn's chill, I wander as a guest; 
In life's long span, ill and lone, I climb this tower. 
Hardship and bitter regret have whitened my temples thick with frost; 
Now downcast, I've just ceased drinking my rough, turbid wine."}

