{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "A Morning Farewell to Yuan Er on His Mission to Anxi

The morning rain in Wei City wets the light dust;
The inn is green, the willow's colors fresh.
I urge you, drain one more cup of wine—
West of Yang Pass, you'll have no old friends left."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My old friend bids farewell to the west at Yellow Crane Tower,  
Amid the misty blossoms of March, he sails down to Yangzhou.  
His lone sail, a distant shadow, vanishes into the blue void;  
All I see is the Yangtze River flowing to the edge of the sky."}

{"source": {"title": "鹿柴", "author": "王维", "text": "空山不见人，但闻人语响。
返景入深林，复照青苔上。"}, "translation": "No one is seen upon the empty mountain;
only the sound of voices carries through.
Slanting light reaches into the deep forest,
and shines again upon the green moss."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "A Spring View
by Du Fu

The nation is broken, hills and rivers remain;
In the city, spring comes, grass and trees grow wild.
Moved by the season, flowers splash with tears;
Hating parting, birds startle the heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three straight months;
A letter from home would be worth ten thousand gold.
I scratch my white hair, it grows ever shorter,
I can hardly hold it with a pin."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "Morning rain in Weicheng has settled the light dust;
At the inn, the willows gleam newly green.
I urge you now to finish one more cup of wine—
West of Yang Pass, no old friends are seen."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
