{"source": {"title": "登高", "author": "杜甫", "text": "风急天高猿啸哀，渚清沙白鸟飞回。
无边落木萧萧下，不尽长江滚滚来。
万里悲秋常作客，百年多病独登台。
艰难苦恨繁霜鬓，潦倒新停浊酒杯。"}, "translation": "**登高** · Du Fu

Wind keen and high the sky, gibbons cry with sorrow;
Islet clear, sand white, birds circle in their flight.

Unending fall the leaves, rustling down;
Unceasing rolls the Yangtze, surging on.

Ten thousand miles away, grieving in autumn, forever a guest;
A hundred years of illness, alone I climb this terrace.

Hardship's bitter grief has thickened my frost-white temples;
In ruin, I've lately ceased my cup of cloudy wine."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "# Spring View

The state lies broken; mountains, rivers stay;
Spring fills the city — grasses run wild and deep.
Time stirs the flowers, splashing tears;
Parting makes the birds' cries startle the heart.
Beacon fires have burned three months unceasing;
A letter home outweighs ten thousand gold.
My white hair scratches ever thinner —
So thin it can no longer hold a pin in place."}

{"source": {"title": "山居秋暝", "author": "王维", "text": "空山新雨后，天气晚来秋。
明月松间照，清泉石上流。
竹喧归浣女，莲动下渔舟。
随意春芳歇，王孙自可留。"}, "translation": "**Mountain Dwelling on an Autumn Evening**

After fresh rain on empty mountains, the evening settles into autumn.
Moonlight filters through the pines; a clear spring slips over stones.
Bamboo rustles — washerwomen heading home;
Lotus stirs — a fishing boat slips away.
Let spring's blossoms fade at their own will;
A man of noble heart may well remain here."}

