{"source": {"title": "武陵春·春晚", "author": "李清照", "text": "风住尘香花已尽，日晚倦梳头。
物是人非事事休，欲语泪先流。
闻说双溪春尚好，也拟泛轻舟。
只恐双溪舴艋舟，载不动许多愁。"}, "translation": "Spring Evening at Wuling Spring  
The wind has stilled, the fragrance of dust-laden flowers is gone;  
At dusk, weary, I no longer care to comb my hair.  
All things remain, yet people are changed—every matter now in vain;  
Before I speak, tears have already flowed.  

I’ve heard that Twin Creeks in spring are still fair and bright;  
I’d even plan to float on a light, small boat.  
Yet fear grips me—this tiny skiff of Twin Creeks  
Cannot bear the weight of so much sorrow."}

